BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:It's Raining Queens: Martha Wash and Marsha Warfield
DTSTART:20261114T040000Z
DTEND:20261114T060000Z
DTSTAMP:20261112T192933Z
UID:rZ7HnEZ1AfGb77
CATEGORIES:concert,free
DESCRIPTION:https://www.ticketweb.com/event/its-raining-queens-martha-wash
 -feinsteins-at-the-nikko-tickets/14318104\nVenue: Feinstein's at The Nikko
 \nLocation: 222 Mason Street\, San Francisco\, CA\nPrice: Free\nGenres: Mu
 sic\, Dance/Electronic\, Dance Pop\nCategories: concert\, free\nSource: ti
 cketmaster/music\n\nIt's Raining Queens™: Starring Martha Wash & Marsha 
 Warfield Two legends. Two San Francisco connections. One unforgettable nig
 ht. Feinstein's at the Nikko presents It's Raining Queens™: Starring Mar
 tha Wash and Marsha Warfield live on Friday\, November 13\, 2026\, in San 
 Francisco. Wash and Warfield move between music\, laughter\, and personal 
 stories with the ease of two accomplished performers who have nothing left
  to prove and every reason to enjoy the moment. For both legendary perform
 ers\, this engagement represents a meaningful return to a city connected t
 o the beginnings of their remarkable careers. Martha Wash was born and rai
 sed in San Francisco\, where her extraordinary journey began. She first ga
 ined recognition singing alongside the legendary Sylvester as one half of 
 Two Tons O' Fun before achieving international success with The Weather Gi
 rls. A two-time Grammy nominee\, Wash is the powerhouse voice behind multi
 -platinum recordings with The Weather Girls\, Black Box\, and C+C Music Fa
 ctory---a catalog that helped shape dance floors and pop radio around the 
 world and continues to inspire generations. Marsha Warfield's connection t
 o San Francisco dates back to an important early breakthrough in her comed
 y career. In 1979\, she won the San Francisco International Comedy Competi
 tion\, becoming the contest's first Black winner and first female winner. 
 Warfield also worked as a writer and performer on Richard Pryor's groundbr
 eaking television variety series\, The Richard Pryor Show
LOCATION:222 Mason Street\, San Francisco\, CA
URL:https://www.ticketweb.com/event/its-raining-queens-martha-wash-feinste
 ins-at-the-nikko-tickets/14318104
END:VEVENT
